  "digest": "# ENERGY \u2014 sector digest, ISO week 2026-W46\n\n**Coverage changes.** Seven initiations published: CGAS (BUY, Rp158), HITS (BUY, Rp192), MINE (BUY, Rp732), SOCI (HOLD, Rp439), GTSI (SELL, Rp12), HILL (SELL, Rp8) and MTFN (SELL, Rp1). Four updates: DOID moved to BUY Rp187 from REDUCE after the D&A and cash-cost restatement; MBAP to ADD Rp1,962 from HOLD after 9M; ITMG cut twice, HOLD Rp21,982 to SELL Rp16,351 on the Q3 print; SMMT held SELL at Rp1,169 on results. IATA published v6 BUY Rp95 on 9 November, then parked. Book: 33 published, 37 parked, 10 queued [coverage state].\n\n**Deck moves.** No forecast variable was re-reviewed. The coal deck is unchanged since the 5 November ICI-4 review: Newcastle spot US$150.35 sits 27% above FY2027E 118.0, HBA 126.81 (October), ICI-3 still needs_source [coal S19/S14]. Oil's daily marks refreshed to 13 November: Brent US$95.89 and WTI US$88.45, still ~14% over the FY2027E 84.0 path [oil deck]. October ICP printed US$117.24 but the deck still carries September's 112.81 \u2014 to be sourced. Macro spot USD/IDR 18,190; konglo unchanged [macro deck].\n\n**Material news.** DSI's NADI export portal is socialised from 15 November ahead of mandatory coal/CPO/ferroalloy exports from 1 January 2027 [1f98ac7f1075501c; 5ad61add23a0c3c4]. The 2027 RKAB submission deadline is 15 November and uncertainty is pressuring coal names [9fec3efd6f7ba01f; 7007c0fe342a13bb]; PLN's 2027 coal requirement is 173 Mt [9137f6d380b11176]. ITMG booked 9M net profit US$138m (+25%) [a4fb87d7a824fd5d] and declared a Rp1,286 interim dividend at 70% payout [34951a98c5296358]. AKRA took over BP's entire Indonesian fuel-station business [737c3a1894d89d55]; RAJA bought 90% of LNG-vessel firm Kapalindo [d5f3e75083d819fb] and was removed from MSCI's Global Small Cap index [ce6fdb9748402de8]. CBRE plans a 48bn-share rights issue converting Rp858.59bn of debt [bccac87022ab57dd]. Fitch cut BUMA to CCC- [86d36335c7a65c7a].\n\n**What to watch.** The 15 November RKAB deadline and the NADI portal session; BYAN's 23 November EGMS; DSI's fee and reference-price mechanics before go-live; and the 37-name parked backlog, including RAJA, CBRE, AKRA and PGAS.\n\n*Research only; not a recommendation to act.*",
